{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1347344-a-tribe-fallen","id":1347344,"title":"A Tribe Fallen","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-09T16:38:21-08:00","id":1347344,"title":"A Tribe Fallen","content":"It's quiet in here, so I figured I'd throw out an idea to maybe get people's juices flowing:<br /> <br /> If another tribe were to fall to the Wyrm (or Weaver but that's a bit of a 1-horse race) within, let's say, the next decade, who do y'all think it would be?<br /> <br /> For my money, I'd guess either the Red Talons, Get of Fenris, or Wendigo<br /> <br /> As a secondary point I suppose, here's something that could be neat. For an alt-WoD setting, what tribe would you like to see fall to the Wyrm either instead of or along with the White Howlers? Also, would you ever consider having a tribe, such as the Red Talons for example, fall to the Wyld?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T16:41:26-08:00","id":1347345,"title":"","content":"Black Furies might \u201cfall\u201d to the Wyld, but that wouldn\u2019t necessarily be a bad thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T16:44:13-08:00","id":1347346,"title":"","content":"I'd agree that it would probably be more welcome to the Nation then another victory for the Wyrm, although I don't think Wyld-tainted garou are going to be a very good thing for the Garou Nation in the long run either.<br /> <br /> I'd imagine that if they became aspects of a mad Wyld the way that the other members of the triat are mad, they'd probably be just as naturally destructive as they are creative, which may have the adverse effect of feeding the Wyrm, though it would probably help in combatting the Weaver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T17:35:00-08:00","id":1347354,"title":"","content":"Glass-Walkers will definitely fall to the Weaver soon. Some tribe-members already revere it if you want to Headcanon it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T18:13:58-08:00","id":1347360,"title":"","content":"Aye, there's really no contest when it comes to tribes falling to the Weaver, the Glass Walkers are far and away in that count. The only ones I can think that might even kinda be in contention as well might be the Bone Gnawers, Children of Gaia, Shadow Lords, &amp; Silver Fangs. The former two because of proximity to humanity (scions of the Weaver that they are) and the latter because of their near religious obsession with hierarchy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T20:56:25-08:00","id":1347396,"title":"","content":"Bone Gnawers.<br /> <br /> There's various signs that there is something serious wrong with the tribe. It doesn't pay much attention to the Litany. It makes lot of deals with vampires. Their totem, Rat, is acting increasingly strangely. A large number of the tribe (the Rabble), have effectively abandoned the struggle for Gaia. There is large enough numbers of Man Eaters that it is a camp of the tribe. <br /> <br /> Now, most of the evidence dates from the first/second edition era which presented a more multi-faceted depiction of the tribes. Much of the wrong found in the Gnawers (and that of other tribes as well) was jettisoned in Revised edition which became more explicitly heroic high fantasy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T22:36:54-08:00","id":1347409,"title":"","content":"That's very fair and that actually makes me wanna ask a question because I hadn't known that some of those kind of aspects had been dropped from 2e.<br /> <br /> (I also feel vindicated for the Time of Judgement chronicle I'm running where I chose the Bone Gnawers as the tribe to fall X D)<br /> <br /> What other sort of tribe lore of that kind do you know about that got dropped going into revised?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T05:48:11-08:00","id":1347456,"title":"","content":"Yes, but I read somewhere that the Wyld is the only member of the Triat that was not driven insane the way the Weaver and the Wyrm were. On the other hand, the Wyld is not really a benevolent mother goddess the way Gaia is either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T20:13:04-08:00","id":1347606,"title":"","content":"Aye, as it is currently the Wyld is the most Gaia friendly member of the triat but even then the Wyld can and does inadvertently undercut and injure Gaian interests purely as a force of unbridled creation and expression.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T12:10:20-08:00","id":1347728,"title":"","content":"Very true.<br /> <br /> Random question: what do you think of the idea of the Black Furies taking the moon goddess Artemis as their Totem instead of Pegasus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T12:43:07-08:00","id":1347736,"title":"","content":"I could certainly see it and it would make sense, although part of me wonders if it might be seen as too overt a connection to Luna and be looked down upon as vying for prefential treatment.<br /> <br /> Honestly though, I can definitely see an alt-WoD with Artemis as the Black Fury tribal totem, though I do think Pegasus is neat and has cool lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T12:53:49-08:00","id":1347739,"title":"","content":"That's a very good point.<br /> <br /> I read the Black Fury Tribebook (along with the Silver Fangs and the Shadow Lords, they're my fave tribe) and it mentioned something about Artemis being their original Totem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T13:22:30-08:00","id":1347747,"title":"","content":"Huh, I did not know that. Well hey, all the more reason that it could be an interesting setting exploration.<br /> <br /> The first difference that comes to mind for me is that Artemis might not share Pegasus' more forgiving policy towards male metis, given I believe that part of that came from Pegasus having sympathy to them as a 'fellow gelded'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T13:29:14-08:00","id":1347751,"title":"","content":"Very good point. Also, Artemis was a virgin goddess, so she might encourage the Black Furies to be even more androphobic than they currently are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T18:05:02-08:00","id":1348091,"title":"","content":"Aye, that is certainly a possibility, although I'll admit that I don't know enough about everything the mythological Artemis had going on for sure to know all the ways she might affect the tribe's altered development.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T23:10:25-08:00","id":1348797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1347344-a-tribe-fallen?p=1347409#post1347409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What other sort of tribe lore of that kind do you know about that got dropped going into revised?</div> </div> </div> </div>Almost every tribe had a camp that was &quot;Wyrmish&quot; - it was engaged in an activity forbidden by the Litany, implied to be doing the Wyrm's bidding in some way, or involved in activity that could be corrupting. All of those camps seemed to have been eliminated in Revised material or massively downplayed.<br /> <br /> They were many camps trying to overthrow or replace the leadership of the Silver Fangs. Not only the Shadow Lords, there were camps in the Get of Fenris, Children of Gaia, Stargazers,and even an allied faction among the Red Talons and Wendigo. Even the Black Furies were spying on them. And there was a group of former Silver Packs who were working to bring down the Silver Fangs because they knew the Fang's rulings were not helping the Nation. And on the other side, there was an implied element of the setting that the Glass Walkers were supporting the Silver Fangs simply in order to win them over against the other tribes. The default assumption in the material wasn't that the Silver Fangs were failing, but that they had already failed.<br /> <br /> There were multiple tribes that had secret dealings with vampires one way or the other. This was more or less part of an attempt to facilitate crossover games in the early editions. Of course, such dealings would need to be kept secret, but it seemed to be &quot;normal&quot; that various tribes had routine, if limited, dealings with individual vampires.<br /> <br /> Things were more complicated in general and revealed the distance between the idealism of the Litany, and what actually was happening in the Garou Nation. There was heavy, heavy conflict within each tribe and between the tribes. It gave lots of hooks for an ST to develop plot. Revised scrubbed out a lot of the complicating factors and presented a much more idealistic portrayal so that Lawful Good could get on the metaplot railroad. I think a major reason for it was that many players did not want a setting that was implied to be moderately corrupt, but wanted their favorite tribe to stalwart defenders of Gaia that would in no way ever tolerate anything than strict adherence to the Litany (as they interpreted it).<br /> <br /> I think the Revised era metaplot where all this internal conflict was overcome (sometimes way too easily by handwaving things) is perfectly fine for an individual chronicle. It is a valid choice and can be a great deal of fun. But there are also other choices were just as valid and as fun in different ways. The main reason I don't like metaplot of any kind, is that it cuts off ST choices and forces players to make the decision to either change what they've done to fit into new material, or abandon supporting the game line because it diverges more and more from what they've done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T14:53:29-08:00","id":1348934,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11637_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11637\" data-vbnamecard=\"11637\">Gryffon15</a> are you Scottish? Or Irish? (You say \u201cAye\u201d a lot \ud83d\ude0a.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T04:12:21-08:00","id":1349047,"title":"","content":"That's all very fair Black Fox and it makes me wanna go back and read some of the early tribe books now. I usually had just read revised era stuff because from everything I had heard, that's where a lot of lore had been streamlined and made internally coherent.<br /> <br /> Also nah, aside from various hereditary questions, I'm several generations in American. I just use stuff like &quot;aye&quot; and &quot;y'all&quot; because I think their useful linguistically and I've just picked up the habit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T09:40:00-08:00","id":1349101,"title":"","content":"It wasn't just in the tribebooks (although that is where the camps are). The first edition Storyteller Handbook has a lot of good information, and there's some good things spread about in other early edition material. <br /> <br /> In Rage Across Russia, we learn about the Typhon spirit, one of Grandfather Thunder's brood, betraying him and leading the septs where he is caern totem, and his packs, to the Wyrm. Yet when Typhon is mentioned in the revised Shadow Lord tribebook, we just get a revised totem description and nothing about it leading its children to the Wyrm. While it is possible this was because that &quot;secret&quot; was meant for ST's eyes only and therefore wouldn't be in the player-oriented tribebook, most likely the game just dropped the idea.<br /> <br /> If you look at the description of the Sept of the Green in the original corebooks and other setting material where it applied, the Bone Gnawers who run the sept do not come off well in regards to your normal operation of the sept. Only one moot per year is seriously planned, and the rest are completely disorganized affairs. It's not surprising that we then learn there is an active conspiracy to remove the Bone Gnawers from leadership. If you want proof that the Bone Gnawers don't take their commitments to Gaia seriously, there is immediate proof there. Yet the tribebook mostly ignores that in favor of showing how the Bone Gnawers are serious about that. Granted, I understand the reason for that - most PCs will likely want to play a Gnawer that is just as committed to Gaia as his fellow PCs from other tribes. So that aspect needs to be emphasized. But we get very little about the HALF of the tribe that doesn't (mentioned as the Rabble and then dismissed, even though it numbers HALF the tribe). Shouldn't we get more details about them and how it impacts the tribe?<br /> <br /> In very early second edition, when crossover was encouraged, we get information about the Sabbat's <i>allies</i> with the &quot;Lupines&quot;. in the Sabbat Player's Guide, Bone Gnawers are mentioned as helping specific packs. Another ally is a small group of Native American shamans called the Penumbra of Gray Squirrels, which also helps some tribes of Lupines. While no further detail is provided, to my ears this sounds like a group of Uktena and Wendigo kinfolk sorcerers that help certain Sabbat nomad packs kill the other tribes. This isn't mentioned anywhere in Werewolf.<br /> <br /> Likewise, if we look at Rage Across New York and read the Characters section, we get a whole lot of intra-Garou conflict and very seriously flawed characters.<ul><li>There's a small camp of man eaters among the Bone Gnawers slowly recruiting numbers, but the tribe knows about it and isn't taking action.</li> <li>The Get of Fenris control a caern, and absolutely prevents any other local Garou from accessing it. Just because.</li> <li>Multiple Garou are shown to have some kind of relationships with vampires - Fianna with the Toreador, Shadow Lords with the Giovanni, and Bone Gnawers with the Nosferatu and Sabbat. While this is all on the down low, it's strong proof that in urban environments, the local vampires make lots of deals with Wyrm minions just as the price of getting by.</li> <li>The current leadership of the Sept of the Green faces potential coups from multiple, independent plots - an internal plot among the sept members who aren't Bone Gnawers, the Silver Fangs who once controlled the caern, and even the Silent Striders.</li> <li>There's lots of important Garou plotting to lead their tribes or septs against the others. Mostly along the lines of &quot;I want a more powerful caern&quot; and they are willing to kill for it.</li> </ul>Needless to say, this kind of internal conflict, while present in every Vampire LARP or online game I've seen, is almost never present in any Werewolf LARP or online game, where &quot;Gaian idealism&quot; is pretty dominant among the PCs and NPCs. There's rarely any conflict between septs, much less within a sept. In other words, players tend to take things like the Litany a lot more seriously than actual NPC Garou did in the books (albeit this is most likely caused by weak leadership in the face of huge threats, rather than an example of how Garou would act when there is strong leadership that can get stuff done).<br /> <br /> We see this kind of internal decay among Garou society all the time in the early edition material. But that would get in the way of the Revised metaplot heroic high fantasy stuff, so it was just eliminated by hand wave, mostly.<br /> <br /> First edition material was very scattershot, and Revised does a better job of trying to make everything more coherent. But it certainly eliminated a lot of things too. Some of the things were just silly and good riddance to it. But they also substantially changed the setting into a different direction of heroic high fantasy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T10:57:42-08:00","id":1349124,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> are the Sons of Typhon fomori from W20 Book of the Wyrm named for the Totem spirit Typhon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T13:17:43-08:00","id":1349155,"title":"","content":"There's a lot of really interesting stuff in there it sounds like and it sounds really interesting as well so I'm gonna do some digging into that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T19:56:53-08:00","id":1349251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1347344-a-tribe-fallen?p=1349124#post1349124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> are the Sons of Typhon fomori from W20 Book of the Wyrm named for the Totem spirit Typhon?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't there has been any official connection, but in early White Wolf material, there was a tendency to imply certain things while not stating it explicitly.<br /> <br /> There are several mentions of Typhon in Werewolf material, but i haven't seen anything that has linked them together. In the original Freak Legionbook, there was the Sons of Typhon from the Tai Upsilon Phi fraternity, and in the same book they mentioned the Serpent Brotherhood (a different kind of fomori) members were favored as recruits, but nothing specifically tied together the Banes from the two. And no formal connection was made. In Rage Across Russia (written in 1993, 2 years before Freak Legion), there was no mention to anything like either of them.<br /> <br /> And of course, the other game lines also made references to a &quot;Typhon&quot; without stating any connection with each other (primarily vampire with the Followers of Set, and Mage).<br /> <br /> One major flaw to making Typhon a betraying spirit in Rage Across Russia, is that anyone with any kind of knowledge of Greek mythology should suspect that a spirit named Typhon is really a bad guy. He's a big dragon like guy that tried to kill Zeus and spawned lots of monsters. But then again, in mythology Fenris is also a bad guy unlike in Werewolf. So people's mileage may differ.<br /> <br /> In my own chronicles, I've gathered these threads together and created a fomori conspiracy behold to their master, Typhon who is a major incarna servant of the Wyrm. They are basically the Illuminati with David Ickes' reptillian conspiracy theory thrown in and access to lots of animal fomori monsters. And instead of Typhon being a spirit beholden to Grandfather Thunder, I substituted a different spirit name (Summanus, the spirit of nocturnal thunder in Roman myth) and made Typhon a patron of that spirit encouraging it to defect and betray Thunder in exchange for more power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T20:12:37-08:00","id":1349253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1347344-a-tribe-fallen?p=1347728#post1347728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Random question: what do you think of the idea of the Black Furies taking the moon goddess Artemis as their Totem instead of Pegasus?</div> </div> </div> </div>Since Artemis is an aspect of Luna, there is a setting implication that she can't be a tribal totem. Luna has already given the Garou her gifts, so she can't favor any specific group over another. Similar restrictions apply to Gaia and Wolf (although to be fair, they might have special kind of avatars that can be totems - Danu and Fenris (and Winter Wolf and Old Wolf of the Woods) respectively, but that is not entirely clear). However, Artemis sent Pegasus to the Black Furies in lieu of her own patronage. Pegasus, as a creature who flies in the air (like the moon) and who is white/silver - the Lunar color, is an effective ersatz replacement.<br /> <br /> At the same time, the tribe's inner leadership obviously digs worshiping Artemis, and it is obvious that would prefer to have her as a totem if they could.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}